# Sprint 25-26 fix: there was no .dockerignore at all, so `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile baked the LOCAL .env file (with dev DB credentials, whatever
# SECRET_KEY happens to be set locally) directly into every image build.
# That's a real secrets-hygiene issue if the image is ever pushed to a
# registry — and it's also *why* every K8s pod ignored the Secret/ConfigMap
# env vars entirely: pydantic-settings' env_file=".env" loading found this
# baked-in file inside the container and used its localhost values instead
# of the real environment. Confirmed by `docker run ... cat /app/.env`
# showing the exact local file. Same rule as .gitignore: never ship .env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Runtime state that shouldn't be baked into an image either.
agent_memory_history/
decision_logs/
weight_history/
agents/plugins/*.py
!agents/plugins/__init__.py
storage/

# Not needed at runtime.
tests/
dashboard/node_modules/
k8s/secret.yaml
